WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.918
Block one has four threads. Thread three

00:00:02.918 --> 00:00:05.335
is outside the seven-output array, so it

00:00:05.335 --> 00:00:07.753
stores minus one in its shared slot.

00:00:12.253 --> 00:00:14.719
Thread two writes output six using the

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:17.184
next slot. What value does it read?

00:00:25.684 --> 00:00:28.111
Thread two reads minus one from thread

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:30.537
three. If thread three returned early, it

00:00:30.537 --> 00:00:32.964
would skip the shared write and the

00:00:32.964 --> 00:00:34.004
required block barrier.
